  "normalization": [
    "Every field is required unless a particular bound kind has no such field. Unknown fields or variants are rejected.",
    "Fixture keys are opaque references, not identifiers whose spelling grants authority. Resolve references exactly through the named fixture map.",
    "Set and unresolved arrays are mathematical sets; comparison is order-insensitive. Exact empty sets permit nothing. Unrestricted is explicit.",
    "Absent, unknown and unavailable remain different unresolved facts; every unresolved fact prevents use and survives conjunction.",
    "Time is unsigned Unix milliseconds, not-before inclusive and expiry exclusive. Remaining delegation depth counts child edges, not current use.",
    "Principal qualification names an exact trust domain, kind and ID. Equal ID text in another domain is another principal. No fixture is authentication evidence.",
    "Source content revision and historical security epoch are separate. Union preserves every distinct observation and every unknown contributor. No stored epoch proves current permission.",
    "Policy attributes and subject completeness remain local to their source observation. A permission exception on one source cannot authorize another source.",
    "Source and policy fixture references in inventories are expanded mechanically. Expected references and bound values are authored independently, never computed by the implementation under test.",
    "All ordinary derivations include all observed content, control and provider-context inputs. They preserve dependency union and conjoin processor/audience bounds without declassification.",
    "Dependency inventory completeness only means no declared unknown contributor. It does not establish subject completeness, a subjectless waiver, caller clearance, current access, or authorization; Elephant policy decisions require separate differential vectors."
  ],
